  <div class="modal-overlay" id="modal-performance-governance" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="performance-governance-title">
    <div class="modal-dialog">
      <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
      <div class="modal-header">
        <span class="modal-eyebrow">01 &middot; Sales career path</span>
        <h2 id="performance-governance-title">Performance review governance</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <p>Governance of the career path is built on two core elements: <b>(1) regular performance reviews</b> to track progress, provide feedback, and guide development, and <b>(2) structured progression and promotion processes</b> to ensure consistent, transparent, and fair advancement decisions.</p>

        <div class="modal-sections">
          <div class="modal-section">
            <span class="section-eyebrow">Element 01</span>
            <h3>Performance review</h3>
            <p><b>Performance is reviewed monthly</b> between the agent and the HUB Leader, as part of the standard sales routines (<a href="#" class="modal-link" data-target-sub="routines">see Section 5</a>). These reviews focus on activity, pipeline, conversion, and overall target achievement, and form the basis for ongoing coaching and development.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="modal-section">
            <span class="section-eyebrow">Element 02</span>
            <h3>Promotion decisions</h3>
            <p>Progression and promotion decisions are aligned with the <b>company-wide performance review cycles</b> (typically every 6 months), ensuring consistency and governance across markets. In addition, <b>off-cycle nominations</b> can be made in cases where agents demonstrate readiness earlier, allowing for flexibility while maintaining a structured and transparent process.</p>

