            <!-- Element 1: Decision-making process -->
            <div class="promo-process-section">
              <div class="section-title">Decision-making process</div>
              <p class="section-intro">In-cycle promotions happen twice a year, preceded by calibrations and people reviews. Off-cycle nominations are available in all other months.</p>
              <div class="promo-process-grid">
                <div class="promo-process-col in-cycle">
                  <h4>In-cycle</h4>
                  <ol class="promo-process-list">
                    <li><span class="item-title">Reviews written</span>Self, leader, peer &amp; upward reviews completed in Hibob.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Calibrations</span>Leaders align on grade distribution and fairness across teams.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">People review meeting</span>Leadership validate final grades, discuss key talent and approve promotions.</li>
                  </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="promo-process-col off-cycle">
                  <h4>Off-cycle</h4>
                  <ol class="promo-process-list">
                    <li><span class="item-title">Identify candidate &amp; confirm eligibility</span>Assess performance, impact, and readiness against next level expectations during monthly performance reviews. Check tenure, time in current role, and consistency of performance ratings.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Complete the nomination form</span>Fill in new role details and provide supporting evidence &mdash; scorecards, grades, KPIs &mdash; mapped to the progression criteria.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Submit &amp; review</span>Submit to the People Partner, followed by a consultation with the Country Leader before a final decision is made.</li>
                  </ol>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Element 2: Decision-makers -->
            <div class="promo-process-section">
              <div class="section-title">Decision-makers</div>
              <p class="section-intro">Every promotion decision &mdash; whether in-cycle or off-cycle &mdash; involves multiple stakeholders to ensure no single person drives the outcome alone.</p>
              <div class="promo-process-grid">
                <div class="promo-process-col in-cycle">
                  <h4>In-cycle &mdash; Four stakeholders</h4>
                  <ol class="promo-process-list">
                    <li><span class="item-title">HUB leader</span>Reviews agent performance and proposes the promotion grade.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Channel leader</span>Validates consistency across the team and channel.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">People partner</span>Mediates calibrations and ensures process compliance.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Country leader</span>Validates consistency across the country.</li>
                  </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="promo-process-col off-cycle">
                  <h4>Off-cycle &mdash; Four stakeholders</h4>
                  <ol class="promo-process-list">
                    <li><span class="item-title">HUB leader</span>Identifies the candidate and champions the case.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Channel leader</span>Reviews the nomination form for completeness and eligibility.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">People partner</span>Reviews and signs off on the nomination before it goes to the Country Leader.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Country leader</span>Final consultation and sign-off before the decision is confirmed.</li>
                  </ol>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Element 3: Data & inputs -->
            <div class="promo-process-section">
              <div class="section-title">Data &amp; inputs</div>
              <p class="section-intro">For in-cycle promotions, the primary input is the performance review grade and qualitative descriptions. For off-cycle promotions this is complemented with the promotion nomination form.</p>
              <div class="promo-process-grid">
                <div class="promo-process-col in-cycle">
                  <h4>In-cycle &mdash; Performance review grade</h4>
                  <p>The grade from the current performance review cycle is the primary &mdash; and only required &mdash; input. It reflects what was delivered, how it was delivered, and includes calibrated feedback from self, manager, peers, and direct reports.</p>
                  <div class="sub-heading">What the grade reflects</div>
                  <ul class="promo-process-bullets">
                    <li>What was delivered &mdash; results and KPIs</li>
                    <li>How it was delivered &mdash; execution, values, and behaviours</li>
                    <li>360 input &mdash; self, manager, peers, and direct reports</li>
                    <li>Calibrated across teams to ensure fairness</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="promo-process-col off-cycle">
                  <h4>Off-cycle &mdash; Nomination form + review grade</h4>
                  <p>Off-cycle nominations require two inputs: the completed promotion nomination form and the agent's most recent performance review grade.</p>
                  <div class="sub-heading">The nomination form must include</div>
                  <ul class="promo-process-bullets">
                    <li>New role details &amp; justification</li>
                    <li>Past scorecards &amp; performance grades</li>
                    <li>KPIs mapped to the progression criteria</li>
                    <li>Examples of behaviours at the next level</li>
                    <li>Most recent performance review grade</li>
                  </ul>
                  <a class="download-link" href="Promotion-Nomination-Form.docx" download>Download nomination form</a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Element 4: Communication -->
            <div class="promo-process-section">
              <div class="section-title">Communication</div>
              <p class="section-intro">Promotions are always communicated privately to the agent first, then celebrated publicly.</p>
              <div class="promo-process-grid">
                <div class="promo-process-col in-cycle">
                  <h4>In-cycle</h4>
                  <ol class="promo-process-list">
                    <li><span class="item-title">Development talk</span>The leader informs the agent privately during their scheduled development talk, delivering the full performance review feedback.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Hibob &mdash; review shared</span>The leader shares the formal review in Hibob, making the final grade and qualitative feedback visible to the agent.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Local Connect announcement</span>The promotion is celebrated publicly at the next local Connect as a team milestone.</li>
                  </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="promo-process-col off-cycle">
                  <h4>Off-cycle</h4>
                  <ol class="promo-process-list">
                    <li><span class="item-title">Leader 1:1</span>The leader informs the agent in a dedicated one-to-one conversation &mdash; before any wider announcement is made.</li>
                    <li><span class="item-title">Local Connect announcement</span>The promotion is announced at the local Connect, recognised as a team milestone alongside in-cycle promotions.</li>
                  </ol>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Modal: Progression criteria -->
  <div class="modal-overlay" id="modal-progression-criteria" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="progression-criteria-title">
    <div class="modal-dialog">
      <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
      <div class="modal-header">
        <span class="modal-eyebrow">01 &middot; Sales career path</span>
        <h2 id="progression-criteria-title">Progression criteria</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <p><b>Time at each level is indicative</b>, rather than fixed. Progression is driven by:</p>
        <ol class="modal-list">
          <li>sustained performance; typically, <b>a minimum four consecutive months of 95&ndash;105% target achievement</b></li>
          <li><b>consistent demonstration of competencies at the next level</b></li>
        </ol>
        <p>High performers may progress faster; others may take longer to consolidate. Criteria are assessed across three dimensions: <b>(1) performance, (2) sales skills, and (3) behaviours</b>.</p>

        <div class="modal-sections">
          <div class="modal-section">
            <span class="section-eyebrow">Dimension 01</span>
            <h3>Performance</h3>
            <p>Performance is measured across three core KPIs:</p>
            <ul class="kpi-list">
              <li>Net Revenue (M1)</li>
              <li>TPV (M1)</li>
              <li>Net Revenue 6M Rolling</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Each country is expected to define targets for each level, based on a target setting model grounded in unit economics. Targets should reflect local market realities and account for ramp-up periods of new joiners.</p>
            <p><b>Progression to the next level requires at least 4 consecutive months of 95&ndash;105% performance</b> across all targets, with a higher bar of 12 months of consistent performance for promotion to BDM and BDE.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="modal-section">
            <span class="section-eyebrow">Dimension 02</span>
            <h3>Sales skills</h3>
            <p>Expectations regarding sales skills evolve <b>from mastering core sales techniques and product knowledge to applying strong commercial judgment, handling more complex deals, and structuring higher-value opportunities</b>.</p>

            <div class="progression-grid">
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">BDR</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Structured pitch</li>
                  <li>Initiates conversations easily</li>
                  <li>Handles basic objections</li>
                  <li>Understands offer &amp; tools</li>
                  <li>Identifies needs &amp; positions solution</li>
                  <li>Adapts pitch to customer</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">S. BDR</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Converts more effectively</li>
                  <li>Stronger product positioning</li>
                  <li>Builds multi-product deals</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">BDM</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Applies commercial judgment on value &amp; pricing</li>
                  <li>Manages customer lifecycle and minimizes churn</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">S. BDM</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Prioritises by business impact</li>
                  <li>Handles complex &amp; non-standard scenarios and negotiations</li>
                  <li>Deep product knowledge across all offers</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">BDE</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>High focus in churn</li>
                  <li>Balances volume with deal quality and customer value</li>
                  <li>Identifies and addresses complex customer needs with tailored solutions</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">S. BDE</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Turns successes into repeatable methods and actionable insights</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="modal-section">
            <span class="section-eyebrow">Dimension 03</span>
            <h3>Behaviours</h3>
            <p>Expectations regarding behaviours shift <b>from individual drive and resilience to greater autonomy, ownership, and leadership</b>. Over time, agents are expected not only to perform but also to influence others, contribute to team success, and shape ways of working.</p>

            <div class="progression-grid">
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">BDR</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Maintains effort despite rejection</li>
                  <li>Tracks own performance vs target</li>
                  <li>Generates leads consistently</li>
                  <li>Follows up until clear outcome</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">S. BDR</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Acts without prompting</li>
                  <li>Seeks &amp; applies feedback</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">BDM</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Thinks in business outcomes</li>
                  <li>Owns territory planning</li>
                  <li>Works independently</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">S. BDM</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Coaches junior team members</li>
                  <li>Drives adoption of new processes and best practices across the team</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">BDE</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Guides others in complex deals</li>
                  <li>Actively coaches in the field</li>
                  <li>Provides structured feedback on products and contributes to pilots and improvements</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="progression-col">
                <div class="progression-arrow">S. BDE</div>
                <ul class="progression-bullets">
                  <li>Steps in on difficult deals</li>
                  <li>Shares practical tips</li>
                  <li>Improves team ways of working</li>
                  <li>Acts as a reliable backup for leadership, ensuring continuity of operations</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Modal: Role evolution -->
  <div class="modal-overlay" id="modal-role-evolution" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="role-evolution-title">
    <div class="modal-dialog">
      <button class="modal-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
