      <div class="modal-body">
        <div class="modal-sections">
          <div class="modal-section">
            <span class="section-eyebrow">Element 01</span>
            <h3>Agent profile</h3>
            <p>The role profile defines what success looks like &mdash; <b>skills, behaviours, and mindsets needed to perform and grow as a field agent</b>. Each profile is <b>built around five dimensions</b>:</p>
            <div class="profile-dims">
              <div class="profile-dim">
                <div class="dim-icon">01</div>
                <h5>Education &amp; Experience</h5>
                <div class="pd-sub">what they have on CV</div>
                <div class="pd-desc">Covers their academic background and relevant work experience</div>
              </div>
              <div class="profile-dim">
                <div class="dim-icon">02</div>
                <h5>Mindset &amp; Attitude</h5>
                <div class="pd-sub">how they think</div>
                <div class="pd-desc">Reflects how they think, approach challenges, and stay motivated in a sales environment</div>
              </div>
              <div class="profile-dim">
                <div class="dim-icon">03</div>
                <h5>Behaviours &amp; Habits</h5>
                <div class="pd-sub">what they do consistently</div>
                <div class="pd-desc">Focuses on the actions and routines they consistently demonstrate day to day</div>
              </div>
              <div class="profile-dim">
                <div class="dim-icon">04</div>
                <h5>Core Skills &amp; Strengths</h5>
                <div class="pd-sub">what they can do</div>
                <div class="pd-desc">Highlights the key capabilities they need to perform effectively in the role</div>
              </div>
              <div class="profile-dim">
                <div class="dim-icon">05</div>
                <h5>Impact &amp; Outcomes</h5>
                <div class="pd-sub">the results they achieve</div>
                <div class="pd-desc">Measures the results they achieve and the value they bring to the business</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p>There are <b>two primary profiles, both serving as entry points into the Field Sales career path: BDA and BDM</b>.</p>
            <div class="modal-cta-row">
              <button type="button" class="modal-cta" data-submodal="bda-profile">See detailed Agent profile &mdash; Entry 1: BDA</button>
              <button type="button" class="modal-cta" data-submodal="bdm-profile">See detailed Agent profile &mdash; Entry 2: BDM</button>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top:14px;">The <b>BDM profile builds on the BDA foundation by keeping the same core expectations</b> and adding additional requirements for a higher level.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="modal-section">
            <span class="section-eyebrow">Element 02</span>
            <h3>Job description</h3>
            <p><b>Based on the agent profile, each market can create and adapt the official job description to local realities</b>. However, a company-wide structure is recommended across three key aspects: (1) role purpose, (2) key responsibilities and deliverables, (3) output and measures of success.</p>
            <p>Click below to see <b>indication of the key elements that should be included</b> in the job description across markets. Based on this framework, <b>each country is expected to define a sample job description, both in English and in the local language</b>, ensuring alignment with the standard structure while reflecting local specifics.</p>
            <div class="modal-cta-row">
              <button type="button" class="modal-cta" data-submodal="bda-jd">See detailed Job description &mdash; Entry 1: BDA</button>
              <button type="button" class="modal-cta" data-submodal="bdm-jd">See detailed Job description &mdash; Entry 2: BDM</button>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top:14px;">At <b>BDA level, the focus is on high activity, prospecting, and consistent execution to drive new customer acquisition</b>. At <b>BDM level, the role shifts toward higher-value opportunities, more complex sales cycles, and building long-term customer value</b>, with greater ownership of territory, pipeline, and commercial decision-making, and success measured not only by volume but also by revenue quality and conversion.</p>
          </div>
